# Allow-list, because the excludes vastly outnumber the includes: the repo is
# 278M and the two images between them need a fraction of it. Sending the rest
# costs a multi-second upload on every build.
#
# Two things to know before editing:
#
#  1. A new path dependency in gleam.toml or server/gleam.toml must be added
#     HERE as well as in the Dockerfile's own COPY, or the deploy fails while
#     CI stays green -- a checkout simply has the package, so `gleam build`
#     cannot catch it. Adding `wire` broke four consecutive api deploys.
#  2. Everything from `!src` down is here for deploy/web.Dockerfile, which now
#     builds dist/ instead of copying a committed one. None of it is
#     convenience: `assets/` holds the vendored wasm compiler and the Brython
#     runtime that the bundle copies into dist/, and package.json + bun.lock
#     are there because the TypeScript worker bundles `sucrase` out of
#     node_modules, so the builder has to `bun install` first. It costs the
#     server image ~18M of context it does not use; one shared ignore file is
#     worth more than shaving that.
*

!fsrs
!wire
!server
!deploy
!src
!assets
!gleam.toml
!manifest.toml
!Makefile
!package.json
!bun.lock

# Build output inside the allowed trees. These are stale host artifacts; the
# image compiles its own.
fsrs/build
wire/build
server/build

# Real secrets, untracked and gitignored. Must never reach an image layer.
server/.env

**/.git
